Cell["\<\
We notice from this plot that the first and largest peak shifts to the right \
as the microphone to speaker distance increases. We also note that the \
amplitude of this pulse response decreases with increased distance. In other \
words sound intensity \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]rolls \
off\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] with distance from the source. We can speculate \
whether this attenuation of the sound signal with distance increases linearly \
or nonlinearly. And if it is nonlinear then what sort of nonlinear function \
of distance is it.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.94838209799085*^9, 
  3.948382370508464*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c18086ae-c051-4c94-8288-\
6fcfbc1ae8d2"]
}, Open  ]],

